@title 3D Heat: the cloud is visible at its default and the slice shows device cuts, not holes
@area 3D
@sizes 1366x768 1920x1080
# Tadjiro: the cloud was too subtle even at its maximum, and the slice had a cut-out where the devices stand. Opacity now stretches over the air's own temperature range (Strength and Contrast sliders) and the cells of a slice inside a device are drawn darker at the device's temperature. Pictures are the evidence (painted overlays): cloud-on and slice-solids.
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-cooling-advice.novo
wait 20
click_text 3D #1
wait 30
click_text Heat #1
wait 20
click_text "Settings for the next run"
wait 10
click_text Quick
wait 10
click_text Simulate #2
wait_s 200
expect_not "Preliminary"
move 700 650
wait 10
shot slice-solids
expect "Slice: darker squares"
click_text Cloud
wait 20
shot cloud-on
check_layout
